# local Claude/zenmux tooling packages — not project source.
# Whole directories, not just the former .agents/skills/* + .context/prompts/*
# subpaths: those narrower rules were already in place, yet 11 files under them
# stayed TRACKED (a .gitignore entry never untracks something already in the
# index — the files were force-added or predate the rule). They were removed
# from the index with `git rm -r --cached` when these lines landed; the working
# copies are untouched on disk.
.agents/
.context/
.superpowers/

# stray root sqlite (real DB lives in data/, gitignored)
open_otc.sqlite

# generated rednote artifacts
docs/rednotes/

# Local scratch + the THIRD-PARTY ISDA reference template. The synthetic corpus
# that used to live here is now TRACKED at backend/app/golden_workflows/documents/,
# because it grades the confirmation-desk-day arena board and a benchmark cannot
# rest on per-environment files (the trap CLAUDE.md records for
# config/agent_channels.yaml). Anything left under docs/confirmations/ is a local
# copy or third-party material — never the graded corpus.
docs/confirmations/

# zhihu article drafts (rewritten from docs/arena reports)
docs/zhihu/

# generated ability-card images (re-renderable from the board data)
docs/arena/cards/

# generated arena blog (rebuildable from posts.yaml + the report markdown)
docs/arena/deploy/build/

# arena readership snapshot (derived from server logs, recomputable)
docs/arena/deploy/stats.json
# NB boards.json is deliberately NOT ignored: the arena DB lives under the
# gitignored data/, so a checkout without it could not rebuild the leaderboard.

# arena run logs: raw stdout of scripts/launch_arena_run.py. Large, per-machine,
# and every score they mention is already in the arena DB and the reports.
logs/
